    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116293" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρα</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤρα</span></b>  (B), only in 
			Ion.
		 form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρη</span></b> , or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤρη</span></b> , some part of a sacrificial
		victim, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάψεται γλῶσσαν, ὀσφῦν δασέαν, ὤρην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					1037.2
				</span></i>
			 (Milet., <span class="entity">iv/iii B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς Ἴωνας λέγειν φασὶ τὴν κωλῆν ὥρην καὶ
			ὡραίαν</span> Sch.HQ <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.89
			</span></i>: but distd. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλῆ, λάψεται . .
				κωλῆν ἀντὶ τῆς ὤρης</span>
			<u>SIG</u>l.c.<i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄωρος</span>(B). (Perh.
			cogn. with Lat. <i>sūra.</i>)</div>
